WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:05.319
The Marvel Cinematic Universe showed audiences
that a man could fly in Iron Man, and since

00:00:05.319 --> 00:00:10.160
then, the slow threading of various superheroes
into a cohesive universe has been pretty amazing.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:14.860
But of all the mighty and astonishing superheroes
that make up Marvel's premiere super-team,

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.600
who is the most incredible?

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:20.380
To settle the question, we're ranking the
most powerful members of the Avengers, starting

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:23.349
from the bottom and ending with the strongest
one there is.

00:00:23.349 --> 00:00:24.519
"Access denied."

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:25.840
"God of Thunder."

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:27.020
"Access denied."

00:00:27.449 --> 00:00:28.440
"Strongest Avenger."

00:00:28.449 --> 00:00:30.240
"Access denied."

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.340
"STRONGEST AVENGER."

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:32.540
"Access denied."

00:00:33.829 --> 00:00:35.379
Hawkeye

00:00:35.379 --> 00:00:39.480
We'll start with the obvious loser on the
team, the Avengers' arrogant archer Clint

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.329
Barton, a.k.a. Hawkeye.

00:00:41.329 --> 00:00:45.210
He's supposedly a super-spy on the level of
Black Widow, but his defining moments in the

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:49.820
movies involve him decidedly not stopping
Thor from getting to his magic hammer, getting

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:55.010
mind controlled by Loki, almost being shot
to death by Ultron, and completely failing

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:56.400
to stop The Vision.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:58.100
"I'm Clint."

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.660
"I don't care."

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:01.660
Quicksilver

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:06.130
Believe it or not, there was a time when Quicksilver,
the white-haired on-again/off-again son of

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:10.680
Magneto, was in two movies just a year apart
from one another—X-Men: Days of Future Past

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:12.630
and Avengers: Age of Ultron.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:16.490
It's certainly hard to believe, since his
appearance in Ultron is so bad that it's rocketed

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:19.070
him down to the sad, lonely Hawkeye tier of
our list.

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:22.880
His power is superspeed, which seems like
it would keep him a bit higher on a list of

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:25.250
most powerful superheroes in the MCU, but
he was also shot to death by Ultron's machine

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:26.250
guns.

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:29.440
Though he may have sacrificed himself to save
Hawkeye and a child, dying because of regular

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:32.640
bullets when you have superspeed is just embarrassing.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:33.660
"You didn't see that coming?"

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:39.320
Black Widow

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:42.320
"Who do you want me to be?"

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:45.259
There's no shame in Black Widow's placement
this far down the list.

00:01:45.259 --> 00:01:49.861
In a world with gods, robots, magic, and aliens,
Black Widow earning a spot on the Avengers'

00:01:49.861 --> 00:01:52.969
roster due to sheer competence is nothing
to be ashamed of.

00:01:52.969 --> 00:01:57.250
Like Hawkeye, she's a super-spy, but unlike
him, she knows better than to use an outdated

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:03.090
weapon that mankind has been developing countermeasures
against for literally thousands of years.

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:06.990
"We're still friends, right?"

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:08.009
Ant-Man

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:11.930
If this list were graded on charm and the
strength of the supporting cast, Paul Rudd's

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:14.640
Scott Lang would easily vault near the top.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:15.640
"What?"

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:17.680
"I wanna know about that tip."

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:19.050
"Oh baby it's on!

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:20.770
It's so on right now."

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:25.620
Unfortunately for the diminutive dynamo, we're
grading on sheer power, and Ant-Man's skills

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:27.080
don't quite stack up.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:31.340
To be fair to the reformed con man, he did
test out growing to a massive size in Civil

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:34.610
War, but no one ever grows to a massive size
to win a fight.

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:38.470
Call it a byproduct of our obsession with
David and Goliath stories, but generally the

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:42.690
only time a character gets bigger is to be
satisfyingly knocked over like an AT-AT on

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:43.690
Hoth.

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:44.690
"But I got the van."

00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:45.400
"It's nice."

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.000
"Yeah, right?"

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:48.800
Falcon

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:52.989
Sam Wilson has both military training and
the coolest flying technology that doesn't

00:02:52.989 --> 00:02:54.340
come with Stark branding.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:58.849
In fact, the only downside to the MCU Falcon
is that they decided to go with a robotic

00:02:58.849 --> 00:03:01.770
drone version of his comics counterpart's
faithful Redwing.

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:06.599
Sure, talking to birds like some sort of high-flying
Aquaman isn't the greatest power, but we're

00:03:06.599 --> 00:03:10.450
getting to the superpowered side of the rankings,
so he'd need something more to rank a bit

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:11.440
higher.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.500
"Don't say it!

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:17.560
"On your left!"

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.819
"Oh, come on."

00:03:19.819 --> 00:03:21.299
Winter Soldier

00:03:21.299 --> 00:03:26.129
He might look like a teen exploring his identity
at Hot Topic, but Buchanan "Bucky" Barnes,

00:03:26.129 --> 00:03:29.200
a.k.a. the Winter Soldier, is a force to be
reckoned with.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:33.450
Tortured and mind-controlled by HYDRA, he's
been on so many secret assassination missions

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:36.530
that his name is a legend in super-spy circles.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:40.750
Add in a super-strong and super-flexible metal
arm that can punch a hole through concrete,

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:44.580
along with a version of the Super Soldier
Serum that powers Captain America, and the

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:46.240
Winter Soldier's a formidable threat.

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:56.159
War Machine

00:03:56.159 --> 00:04:00.760
They say it's good to have friends in high
places, but generally, the most those high-powered

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:04.049
friends can do is get you a job or maybe loan
you a few bucks.

00:04:04.049 --> 00:04:08.129
For James "Rhodey" Rhodes, being best friends
with Tony Stark means that he gets a personalized

00:04:08.129 --> 00:04:12.470
version of Tony's high-tech armor with enough
guns and missiles to start, and finish, a

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:13.280
small war.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.540
Spider-Man

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:27.500
Smart, superpowered, and fitted out with Stark
tech, Spider-Man's a late, but powerful, addition

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:28.700
to the MCU.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:33.190
In his first appearance in the MCU in Civil
War, he's able to disable Winter Soldier and

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:37.500
Falcon, bring down a Giant Man, and even keep
up with Captain America.

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.920
That's a pretty strong opening for the young
superhero.

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:41.440
"It's that Spider-Guy on YouTube right?"

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:43.240
"Call me Spider-Man!"

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:44.360
"Okay, Spider-Man.

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:46.260
Do a flip!

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:47.920
...Yeah!!!!"

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:50.380
Captain America

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:55.290
Captain America's the full package, and we're
not just talking about actor Chris Evans.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:05:00.230
Steve Rogers has superpowers, fighting prowess,
and an indestructible vibranium shield that's

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:04.460
the closest thing to unbreakable that the
MCU has—at least until adamantium shows

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:04.980
up.

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:05.980
(SNIKT)

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:09.850
Plus, if we're counting raw charisma as a
superpower, that's one more advantage for

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:11.540
the star-spangled Avenger.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:12.540
"Captain America!"

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:13.540
"Mr. Lang."

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:14.720
"It's an honor.

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:16.720
I'm shaking your hand too long.

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:18.420
Wow, this is awesome!

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:19.600
Captain America!"

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:23.880
Onscreen, he's handily beaten nearly every
character on this list, whether in fistfights

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:26.520
with Spider-Man or footraces against the Falcon.

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:28.210
"On your left."

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:29.340
"Uh, huh.

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:30.940
On my left, got it."

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:33.560
Iron Man

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:38.530
Iron Man is everyone's favorite genius billionaire
playboy philanthropist, and that's even before

00:05:38.530 --> 00:05:42.870
you get to the laser-blasting, high-tech weaponry
all wrapped up in a suit powered by tech more

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:44.720
powerful than a nuclear reactor.

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:46.560
And that's only in one suit.

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:51.090
There are the dozens that he can control remotely,
or the giant suit he built specifically to

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:53.240
beat down the strongest thing in the world.

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:57.400
While his lack of close combat experience
might seem to drop him a bit lower, the ending

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:01.941
of Civil War shows him fighting Captain America
and the Winter Soldier to a standstill, even

00:06:01.941 --> 00:06:06.080
with a barely functioning suit, so he's more
than earned his spot.

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:09.870
"Yeah, big man in a suit of armor.

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:10.870
Take that off, what are you?"

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:15.030
"Genius, billionaire, playboy, philanthropist."

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:16.450
Black Panther

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:21.110
Tony Stark might be an eccentric rich genius
in America who gets treated like a king, but

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:24.990
he's not an actual king like the Black Panther,
the ruler of Wakanda.

00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:28.730
Like Iron Man, he's got a technologically
advanced suit—though in Black Panther's

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:31.180
case, it's made of nigh-indestructible vibranium.

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:35.650
Plus, he has brilliant kid sister Shuri to
build any gadget he needs.

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:40.050
But Black Panther's also got the fight training
that Stark lacks, along with highly trained

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:44.960
bodyguards, and the backing of an entire country
so technologically advanced it makes New York

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:47.300
City look like fifteenth-century Europe.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:49.590
Plus, the magic of the heart-shaped herb.

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:50.460
Pretty hard to beat.

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:01.760
Scarlet Witch

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:06.120
This is a bit of a tough one, since the Scarlet
Witch of the MCU might be significantly less

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:08.050
powerful than the comics version.

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:12.720
In the comics, the Scarlet Witch is a ridiculously
powerful mutant who was able to completely

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:17.440
erase the mutant genome from the planet with
her chaos magic, but the comics' "No more

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:21.790
mutants" has nothing on Disney's "No mutants
until we buy the rights to the X-Men back."

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:26.720
As a result, the Scarlet Witch of the MCU
uses abilities that run closer to telekinesis

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:30.160
and telepathy than the Chaos Magic of her
comics counterpart.

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:34.220
Even without magic, though, she's a powerful
superheroine, able to take down half the team

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:35.690
under Ultron's orders.

00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:39.700
She might be young and have questionable taste
in robot men, but being the only possible

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:42.400
magic user so far on the Avengers puts her
over the top.

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:51.580
The Vision

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:56.650
In the comics, the Infinity Gems are the most
powerful items in the universe, used in conjunction

00:07:56.650 --> 00:08:01.180
with the Infinity Gauntlet to wield complete
control over basically everything.

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:05.530
While there's not full confirmation that the
MCU will follow suit until the release of

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:10.520
Avengers: Infinity War, it's not a far stretch
to say that the magical MacGuffins are incredibly

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:11.520
powerful.

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:16.090
The Vision, the android based on Tony Stark's
JARVIS AI, has the Mind Stone embedded in

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:21.440
his forehead, giving him the powers of density
manipulation, intangibility, and laser blasts.

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:26.090
Altogether, the combination of a brilliant
AI, laser blasts, and energy derived from

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:31.320
a fundamental power source of the entire Marvel
universe makes The Vision almost godlike.

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:38.260
Thor

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:44.440
Unfortunately for Vision, god-like isn't godly,
and Thor is an actual God.

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:47.540
"You call yourself Lord of Thunder…"

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:49.590
"God of Thunder."

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:54.250
Even if you discount his magic hammer, or
his control of storms, or even his super-strength,

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:58.750
he's the prince of Asgard, a popular scion
of a supremely powerful king who commands

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:00.280
a whole army of gods.

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:04.410
Each one of Thor's many friends and family
members are nearly as strong as he is, living

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:06.820
in a god-filled utopia in space.

00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:07.940
But there is one greater.

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:18.060
The Hulk

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:19.820
"We'll come for you."

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:21.620
"I have an army."

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:22.700
"We have a Hulk."

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:27.321
Bruce Banner's green alter ego has beaten
basically everyone in the entire Marvel Universe

00:09:27.321 --> 00:09:32.120
a few different times, often in literally
earth-shattering ways, and that's just in

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:33.120
the comics.

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:38.650
In the MCU, Hulk's personally beaten the tar
out of Thor, Iron Man, Loki, The Abomination,

00:09:38.650 --> 00:09:43.460
and the entire U.S. Army—and those are just
the characters who've actually bothered to

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:45.290
fight him instead of just running away.

00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:49.940
Out of the MCU's Avengers so far, the Hulk's
powers are truly incredible.

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:57.780
Thanks for watching!

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:00.270
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:00.270 --> 00:10:02.580
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!"

